WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.830
The second trailer for "Ghostbusters: Afterlife"
is finally here, and there's a ton for fans

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.210
to unpack in this glimpse at the latest "Ghostbusters"
story.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:12.440
Here's some of the details only true fans
noticed in the latest "Ghostbusters: Afterlife"

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.440
trailer.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.849
In the trailer, a black and white photo of
the four original Ghostbusters is shown.

00:00:17.849 --> 00:00:20.220
They're posing in front of their firehouse.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.550
This photo appears to have been taken on the
set of the first movie.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:27.509
Based on the clothing they're wearing, it
was probably taken on the day that the Ghostbusters

00:00:27.509 --> 00:00:30.999
were visited by spiteful EPA inspector Walter
Peck.

00:00:30.999 --> 00:00:34.940
He winds up shutting down the containment
unit holding all the ghosts they've captured,

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:39.270
causing an explosion that frees all the trapped
vapors, entities, and slimers.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:44.160
As hundreds of spirits escape and begin creating
mayhem all over New York City, the Ghostbusters

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.160
are arrested.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.830
"Ghostbusters: Afterlife" will focus largely
on characters who are new to the franchise,

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:54.530
but the latest "Ghostbusters: Afterlife" trailer
includes two appearances from some familiar

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:55.530
characters.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.920
The trailer's first cameo comes courtesy of
Annie Potts, who can be seen reprising her

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.850
"Ghostbusters" role as Janine Melnitz.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:05.869
The former Ghostbusters receptionist appears
to be giving Carrie Coon's Callie a tour of

00:01:05.869 --> 00:01:10.079
the creepy farmhouse left to her and her children
by her late father, Egon Spengler.

00:01:10.079 --> 00:01:14.899
"Janine, someone with your qualifications
would have no trouble finding a top flight

00:01:14.899 --> 00:01:20.020
job in either the food service or housekeeping
industries."

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:23.280
Potts doesn't appear again throughout the
rest of the trailer, but her appearance acts

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:27.820
as an efficient way to connect "Afterlife"
to the original two "Ghostbusters" films.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:32.189
The familiar manner in which Janine refers
to Egon also suggests that Janine could possibly

00:01:32.189 --> 00:01:37.259
be the mother of Coon's Callie, which could
potentially make her Egon's wife and partner.

00:01:37.259 --> 00:01:41.729
Janine and Egon did share a romantic spark
in the first "Ghostbusters" film, but Potts'

00:01:41.729 --> 00:01:45.259
character went on to date Louis Tully in "Ghostbusters
2."

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:49.259
Still, it's possible "Afterlife" will reveal
that Janine and Egon ended up getting together

00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:52.509
some time after the events of "Ghostbusters
2."

00:01:52.509 --> 00:01:56.100
Or Janine could just be giving Callie a tour
of the farmhouse as an old family friend.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:00.039
Either way, the scene is a fun nod to the
connection that Janine and Egon had in the

00:02:00.039 --> 00:02:01.170
first "Ghostbusters."

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:05.560
The "Ghostbusters: Afterlife" trailer appears
to give us a few hints as to what evil is

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.060
at the center of the film.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:12.650
When Phoebe peers over the edge of what appears
to be an active volcano, an arm suddenly reaches

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:13.650
out.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:17.790
Sharp-eyed fans may notice that the figure's
electricity-laden arm and spiky hair is reminiscent

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:23.290
of Gozer, the extremely powerful, supernatural
being who was introduced in the original "Ghostbusters"

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:24.290
movie.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:28.120
In the first "Ghostbusters," Gozer takes the
form of the Stay Puft Marshmallow Man and

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:32.790
wreaks havoc on New York City before being
blasted to smithereens by the Ghostbusters.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:37.319
Gozer also had two loyal subjects who were
central to the "Ghostbusters" universe — Vinz

00:02:37.319 --> 00:02:40.189
Clortho the Keymaster and Zuul the Gatekeeper.

00:02:40.189 --> 00:02:45.159
If Gozer does in fact return for "Ghostbusters:
Afterlife," it's possible that its minions

00:02:45.159 --> 00:02:46.159
will return, too.

00:02:47.159 --> 00:02:51.290
The "Afterlife" trailer is partly framed by
a conversation between Callie and Mr. Grooberson

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:55.640
over dinner as the single mother explains
the dynamic she has with her children.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:59.620
She gets on fine with her son Trevor, but
she has a fraught relationship with her daughter

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:00.620
Phoebe.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:04.680
It's not clear whether Callie and Mr. Grooberson
are on a date or not, but it wouldn't be surprising

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:08.330
if their roles are a bit bigger than the trailers
have implied so far.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:13.420
The 1984 film established that two entities
are needed to free Gozer: the Gatekeeper and

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:14.620
the Keymaster.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:19.819
Zuul possesses Dana Barrett in the original,
while Vinz Clortho takes over Louis Tully.

00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:24.090
With Gozer seemingly threatening Summerville
in "Ghostbusters: Afterlife," the malevolent

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:27.829
entity will likely need two new hosts to open
the gateway once again.

00:03:27.829 --> 00:03:31.700
Since Callie and Grooberson have struck up
some kind of rapport, it's possible that the

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:34.390
sequel is setting them up to be the new Gatekeeper
and Keymaster.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:39.799
Officially known as Terror Dogs in the original
film, "Ghostbusters'" iconic monsters look

00:03:39.799 --> 00:03:43.640
like giant, horrifying dogs with horns and
demonic, glowing eyes.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:47.879
The Terror Dogs were used by Gozer to possess
Dana Barrett and Louis Tully, turning them

00:03:47.879 --> 00:03:49.019
into its servants.

00:03:49.019 --> 00:03:52.560
Now, it seems the Terror Dogs are back to
wreak havoc in Summerville.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.579
In the trailer, we see a dog break through
the doors of a Walmart and chase a frightened

00:03:56.579 --> 00:03:59.040
Mr. Grooberson through the parking lot.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.159
We don't know if this dog is Zuul or Vinz
Clortho, or an entirely new creature.

00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:06.530
Either way, it's clear this Terror Dog isn't
likely to play nice.

00:04:07.783 --> 00:04:08.783
"Nice doggy.

00:04:08.783 --> 00:04:10.485
Cute little pooch.

00:04:10.485 --> 00:04:13.532
Maybe I got a milkbone."

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:19.940
Clearly, "Ghostbusters: Afterlife" is leaning
into the mythology of the first movie through

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.940
the apparent returns of both Gozer and the
Terror Dogs.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:27.520
When Egon explains the history of Gozer and
its worshippers, he says that Ivo Shandor

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.780
amassed a cult of nearly a thousand followers
in the 1920s.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:33.500
"They conducted rituals up on the roof.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.860
Bizarre rituals intended to bring about the
end of the world."

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:41.220
Now, it seems like Ivo may have had a back-up
plan in Summerville, Oklahoma.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:44.550
In the "Ghostbusters: Afterlife" trailer,
the mines on the edge of town are called the

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.710
Shandor Mines.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:49.710
The trailer briefly shows Trevor and his friends
exploring the mines, which are filled with

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.639
ominous statues and occult imagery.

00:04:51.639 --> 00:04:56.319
Then, we see a huge cosmic portal swirling
overhead, releasing a horde of ghosts into

00:04:56.319 --> 00:04:57.319
the small town.

00:04:57.319 --> 00:05:01.530
Perhaps Ivo Shandor himself is responsible
for building the mines, or maybe one of his

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:05.789
followers decided to have a backup plan in
place in case their rituals didn't work.

00:05:06.789 --> 00:05:11.500
Perhaps the biggest surprise of the "Ghostbusters:
Afterlife" trailer comes in the last few seconds.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:15.870
After we see an old commercial for the Ghostbusters
playing on YouTube, we see a phone ring, and

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:18.110
Dan Aykroyd's Raymond Stantz picks up.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:22.460
We only see his arms, but we instantly know
it's Ray because of his voice when he answers.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.040
"We're closed."

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:28.669
It looks like the former Ghostbuster is still
running his Occult bookstore, as evidenced

00:05:28.669 --> 00:05:30.850
by a neon sign for the shop on the window.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:35.229
Ray first opened the shop when the Ghostbusters
were served a judicial restraining order between

00:05:35.229 --> 00:05:39.770
the first and second movies, and fans will
definitely be excited to see him back in the

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:40.770
franchise.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.639
"Ray's Occult.

00:05:42.639 --> 00:05:47.000
7:00 on weekdays, midnight on Saturdays.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.210
Thank you."

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:53.009
If you look closely at Ray's arm you'll see
a tattoo that's actually a reference to the

00:05:53.009 --> 00:05:57.139
conversation he had with Winston Zeddemore
in the original film where they talked about

00:05:57.139 --> 00:06:01.060
a bible verse depicting the end of the world
and how it tied into their work.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:08.560
"Maybe the reason we've been so busy lately
is the dead have been rising from the grave."

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:10.900
"How about a little music?"

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.100
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:16.889
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

